    "id": "episode-06-partial-necrosis",
    "title": "Episode 06: Partial Necrosis",
    "type": "Main story",
    "when": "Chapter 6",
    "summary": "Reunion is driven out of Lungmen, but Wei Yenwu's purge of the slums comes to light. FrostNova dies joining Rhodes Island, and Chernobog's core now heads for Lungmen. Some supporting details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "After Reunion is pushed out of the L.G.D. headquarters, Rhodes Island and the L.G.D. launch a joint operation to clear the city. Mephisto turns more of his men into mindless puppets, called the Herd, which attacks anyone nearby, including Reunion's own fighters. Faust is disgusted by this, and he leaves Mephisto. Speculation (no source found yet): He rallies his Phantom Crossbowmen to save as many people as possible from the Herd.",
      "Ch'en and Swire push through the slums to cut off the retreating Reunion forces. Black Raincoats cut down Reunion fighters and thin out the Herd. Ch'en and Swire realize that Wei Yenwu plans to destroy the slums through the Black Raincoats, who were ordered to do it by the censors. Speculation (no source found yet): Three Yanese Imperial Censors watch from nearby, and the slums are almost empty. When Ch'en chases one of the Raincoats to a roof, the soldiers tell her to stop investigating and imply they act with Wei's authority. Swire contacts Lin Yühsia, the daughter of the slums' godfather. Yühsia confirms she is part of Wei's plan to purge the Infected from the slums, so Reunion has no place to hide.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Faust returns to Mephisto to combine their forces, and Mephisto refuses to stop using his Arts. Their history explains why. Mephisto was once a boy named Eno, and Faust was Sasha. Eno was abused by his family and became Infected when a woman forced him to swallow a piece of Originium. Disputed: the draft said his stepmother did this, but the sources we found say only that a woman did. Sasha swallowed Originium too, so they could be Infected together. Talulah took them in, and they took new names.",
      "Faust orders his men to take Mephisto with them. He stays behind and uses his Arts to cover their tracks, and he falls in combat. GreyThroat witnesses his death and reports it to Amiya. Speculation (no source found yet): The L.G.D. crossbowmen are the ones who kill him, and he refuses to fire his own crossbow in return. Amiya and Ch'en then learn that FrostNova's Yeti Squadron has joined Reunion's forces through a passage under the slums.",
      "Meanwhile Kal'tsit and Projekt Red ambush Crownslayer. Crownslayer believes Kal'tsit sold out her father Ilia and the other Sarcophagus researchers to the Ursus government. Kal'tsit lets her attack, then summons Mon3tr and overpowers her. Kal'tsit explains that Sergei betrayed the scientists only because his children, Alex and Misha, were in danger. Speculation (no source found yet): The scientists had sealed the Sarcophagus, which stopped Ursus from using its power for war. Kal'tsit tells Crownslayer to leave Reunion and her path of revenge, and Crownslayer leaves the city as ordered and seemingly deserts Reunion.",
      "Nine, Ch'en's senior in the L.G.D., decides to leave Lungmen and join Reunion. Speculation (no source found yet): She does so after witnessing Wei Yenwu's massacre, and she was acting as a Reunion informant. Ch'en comes up with an idea to steer the Yeti Squadron toward the Black Raincoats so the two can be confronted at once. The Yeti Squadron holds off the Raincoats. Speculation (no source found yet): FrostNova seals off several roads with her Arts until she collapses from the strain. Her sacrifice lets the other Reunion groups escape, and the Yeti Squad instructs the rest of Reunion to take her back to Chernobog so she can be with Patriot when she dies.",
      "Rhodes Island finds FrostNova again. Speculation (no source found yet): Her Oripathy has reached a severe stage, where Originium shards float around her body, and she overpowers Amiya, Blaze, and GreyThroat together. During the battle she admits that Reunion has failed to help the Infected. Speculation: She says she and her brothers died for nothing. She challenges Rhodes Island to defeat her and Talulah. Rhodes Island defeats her, and the Doctor stays with her in her last moments. FrostNova regrets joining Reunion and the atrocities she committed. She asks the Doctor to save the real Talulah from this destructive path, joins Rhodes Island, and dies in the Doctor's arms.",
      "Sources say the Shadow Guards may have carried out a purge of the Infected in the slums, disposing of the bodies in the sewers under cover of the fighting between Reunion and the joint forces. Ch'en keeps investigating and finds corpses of Infected in the sewers. Swire had warned her against it, but the corpses confirm that many Infected were killed. Ch'en is furious, and she moves to confront Wei Yenwu directly.",
      "Amiya meets Wei to cancel the contract between Rhodes Island and Lungmen, citing a lack of transparency. Ch'en barges in, accusing Wei of eradicating the Infected of Lungmen and of killing Talulah's father. Wei tells her to stand down, but Kal'tsit arrives with news that Talulah has turned Chernobog's urban core toward Lungmen. It will collide with the city in thirty-six hours. The core is broadcasting identification codes to all of Lungmen's sub-cities, all with the same message: \"This city still belongs to Ursus.\""
    ],
