    "id": "episode-13-the-whirlpool-that-is-passion",
    "title": "Episode 13: The Whirlpool that is Passion",
    "type": "Main story",
    "when": "Chapter 13",
    "summary": "Londinium falls to the Sarkaz, and the Duchess of Windermere dies. Siege organizes her followers into a unit that the sources connect to the Exemplars. At Brentwood the Sanguinarch is lost, dissolving into the sea beyond civilization. Some details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Londinium has fallen to the Sarkaz. Norport formally declares the occupation, and the Shard's Catastrophic clouds keep the Grand Dukes' armies from reaching the capital. Wellington's troops are forced to retreat from the Nachzehrers. Windermere withdraws, taking Rhodes Island, the Glasgow Gang, and the Norport refugees with her aboard her battleship. The Londinium Defence Forces that allied with the Military Commission are disbanded, and Feist and Rockrock go out to track Sarkaz supply lines.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Windermere's troops are ambushed in a valley. The Confessarii and the Sanguinarch infiltrate the landship, and the newly reborn Damazti Cluster helps set the trap that mortally wounds the Duchess with blood Arts. Delphine gets one last moment with her mother. Meanwhile Salus kidnaps Amiya, and the Doctor pursues alone. In a Sarkaz cave, Salus tries to take the King of Sarkaz crown from Amiya, but Amiya's subconscious repels her, and Logos and Ascalon force Salus to retreat.",
      "Hoederer, W, and Ines climb the Feranmut's bones, and Hoederer takes Ulšulah's pocket watch to search it for the Feranmut's consciousness. Disputed: the draft placed the Lich Ermengarde in this scene and said Ermengarde recognized the altars as Vampire Arts Circles. The source does not mention Ermengarde here. It shows Hoederer seeing a vision of a young vampire warning the Feranmut away from Kazdel. Speculation (no source found yet): Logos finds similar altars, and Paprika's squad lets him commandeer their vehicle. He notes that the altars were not built with ordinary Originium. Meanwhile, Nowell, an Ageless who hates his own immortality, joins the refugees Reunion is gathering.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): After the Duchess's death, Windermere's staff orders the troops to report to Irnclad Galavae, leaving the Glasgow Gang, most Norport refugees, and infected soldiers behind. Siege and Delphine lead them on foot until Shearer, impatient, is struck by Siege. Delphine, in her mother's garb, stops him. A Trilby Asher then asks again for the Sighs of Kings, and Siege answers that she will only work with Caster if they are used on the front lines. He hands her an SOS from Tempest Platoon at Chetleigh, where Siege's group helps hold the town. There she nearly dies detonating a Sarkaz altar, which devastates the Sarkaz forces.",
      "Siege decides to organize those who followed her, and the sources connect this to the Exemplars, a Victorian unit. Disputed: the draft called the Exemplars a legendary unit disbanded after the War of the Four Nations. The source says the Exemplars were disbanded by broadcast two months after the end of a war, and it calls the earlier conflict the Battle of the Four Emperors. Speculation (no source found yet): Siege finds an IFF beacon bearing the identification code of the Exemplars. She forms her own platoon, free of the Grand Dukes, and unites the Glasgow Gang, the Norport refugees, and the abandoned Victorian soldiers under the reformed Exemplars. Meanwhile Amiya, unconscious, sees herself becoming the Lord of Fiends who enslaves Terra. She rejects that fate and vows to lead both the Sarkaz and the other Terrans, the role Theresa entrusted to her.",
      "Guard negotiates with the Victorian Reunion leader, Mays, over how to treat non-Infected refugees. Speculation (no source found yet): An agitated non-Infected reveals that Infected fighters killed an innocent Sarkaz, who was himself Infected, and the room holding Infected corpses fills with active Originium dust. Disputed: the draft set the scene in an abandoned winery. The source places it in an occupied distillery hidden in the forest. Speculation (no source found yet): Guard orders the evacuation, but Mays goes back for crude suppressants. Disputed: the draft said suppressants. The source says Guard sacrifices himself to save Mays and a collection of petals she used for making medicine. An explosion is heard outside, and Guard dies in the flames. He leaves a recorded message to Reunion questioning whether they are truly fighting for all the infected. Disputed: the draft said all the oppressed. The source says all the infected.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Nine takes Guard's question as her goal and declares that Reunion is for everyone oppressed, whatever their Oripathy. Talulah wakes from her guilt when she hears it. Meanwhile Qui'sartuštaj hypnotizes Nightingale at Shining's safehouse. Shining learns that the Confessarii plan to become the eternal King of Sarkaz by killing Nightingale, an artificial vessel, and passing Shining's father's soul to her brother. Nightingale says she is glad to be on Shining's side as a human, not a vessel. Qui'sartuštaj then vanishes with her.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): The allies find the Vampire altars concentrated in Brentwood, where villagers built a large altar. When it is complete, it drains the villagers' blood and turns them into worm-like creatures blessed by the Sanguinarch. Magdelene nearly becomes a victim until Feist and Rockrock rescue her. Lettou kills himself in front of the Sanguinarch, splashing his blood on the Sanguinarch's robe. Disputed: the draft said the Sanguinarch then took control of the altars and a Feranmut skeleton in the Military Commission's basement. The source says Ulšulah and the Sanguinarch's blood controlled the Feranmut. Speculation (no source found yet): Theresis warns him to hide his weakness.",
      "The allies capture the Feranmut and climb onto the Lifebone to take control of its consciousness. Amiya and Logos fight the Sanguinarch on the skeleton, which drifts toward an endless sea beyond civilization. Amiya denounces the Court of Blood. Hoederer, Ines, W, and Amiya knock him off the Lifebone, and he dissolves into the dirge. His final words are: \"I'll be waiting for you behind the curtain of ruin.\" Speculation (no source found yet): He is trapped forever in the flow of time. Hoederer makes a wager with the Feranmut about who will win the Londinium crisis. Kal'tsit then learns that the Sarkaz's real goal is to activate the Shard through the first Originium, the source of Oripathy.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Eblana and Talulah, the two Dracos of Victoria, meet in a fierce clash. Eblana offers Talulah a place fighting for the Tarans in exchange for leaving the Infected alone, but Talulah refuses. Eblana lets the Reunion fighters go, buying the Tarans time. Caster persuades Wellington to cooperate, with the Duke of Gododdin as mediator. Meanwhile an Emperor's Blade from Ursus quietly enters Victoria."
    ],
